### What is happening?

When routing a non-native circuit to a physical layout, some operations, such as `Barrier` and `Delay` are added to all qubits in the backend. This can be an issue if some of these qubits are marked as faulty, and should instead be excluded. 


### How can we reproduce the issue?

The following circuit
```python
from qiskit.providers.fake_provider.backends.jakarta import FakeJakarta
from qiskit import qasm3
backend = FakeJakarta()
qc = QuantumCircuit(4, 1)
qc.h(0)
qc.cx(0, 2)
qc.measure(0,0)
transpiled_circuit = transpile(qc, backend, initial_layout=list(range(4)))

exporter = qasm3.Exporter(
    disable_constants=True , basis_gates=backend.configuration().basis_gates, 
)
print(qasm3_txt_a := exporter.dumps(transpiled_circuit))
```
where the coupling map of the `backend` does not include the `[0,2]` edge

returns 
```
OPENQASM 3;
include "stdgates.inc";
bit[1] c;
rz(1.5707963267948966) $0;
sx $0;
rz(1.5707963267948966) $0;
cx $0, $1;
cx $1, $0;
cx $0, $1;
cx $1, $2;
barrier $1, $0, $2, $3, $4, $5, $6;
c[0] = measure $1;
```

with a `Barrier` applied on all qubits in the backend, including the idle ones (here 4 to 6) and potentially those that are not operational. 




### What should happen?

Operations should not be applied on non-used qubits. 

If any of the additional qubits is non-operational, the circuit will not run on the backend where those qubits may not be defined. 
If any of the additional qubits is not in use, it will not be marked as idle, negating the fix in  https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-ibm-provider/pull/725 to avoid padding on idle qubits.

